      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "For a typical home in Utah, a complete roof replacement generally costs between $10,000 and $20,000. However, pricing can swing from $8,000 to over $30,000 depending heavily on your home\u2019s footprint, roof complexity, and the materials used .",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "between $10,000 and $20,000"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost by Material (2,000 Sq. Ft. Home)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Roofers measure projects by \"squares\" (1 square = 100 square feet). Because of pitch and overhangs, a 2,000 sq. ft. home footprint usually requires roughly 2,800 to 3,500 square feet of actual roofing material.",
