      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Utah-Specific Cost Drivers"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Regional Labor Variances: Labor rates in Salt Lake County and the Utah Valley are higher due to population growth, typically adding $1,000 to $2,000 to a project compared to Cache, Weber, or Davis counties.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Severe Weather Modifications: In heavy snow zones like Park City and Heber, building codes require extensive ice and water shields. High wind zones (like near the canyon mouths) often require upgraded shingles rated for 130 MPH.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              7,
              8,
              9
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "The \"Tear-Off\" Factor: If your existing roof has multiple layers of old shingles, contractors will charge an extra $75 to $150 per square to tear down and dispose of them.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5,
              10
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Seasonality: High-elevation mountain roofing is restricted to May\u2013October. Scheduling your replacement during the shoulder seasons (March/April or October/November) can sometimes secure more flexible pricing.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              7,
              11
            ]
          }
        ]
